<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Deliberately dependency-free: this is the abstraction package generic rig-control and
       channel-sensing consumers (loggers, digimode apps, a MAC layer or CSMA gate) can take
       without inheriting any AX.25 stack. Backends and drivers (M0LTE.Rig.Hamlib,
       M0LTE.Rig.Flrig, M0LTE.Tait.Ccdi) depend on this; nothing here depends on them. -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Title>M0LTE.Rig - rig-control abstractions: station control (CAT) and channel sensing</Title>
    <Description>Two seams over an amateur-radio transceiver, both dependency-free and capability-probed: IRigControl, the station-control (CAT) seam for frequency, mode, PTT and SWR/RF-power metering; and IRadioControl, the channel-sensing seam for RSSI, hardware carrier-sense (DCD) edges and transmitter keying, plus IRadioSideChannel for radio-native small-datagram messaging. RigRadioControl bridges any IRigControl to IRadioControl by polling its receive-side reads. Implementations: M0LTE.Rig.Hamlib and M0LTE.Rig.Flrig for IRigControl; M0LTE.Tait.Ccdi implements both seams natively for Tait TM8100/TM8200 radios. Source: github.com/M0LTE/M0LTE.Rig.</Description>
    <PackageTags>amateur-radio;rig-control;cat;hamlib;flrig;transceiver;swr;rssi;dcd;ptt;carrier-sense</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
